1228:Oh, Hinata, you're here! Just in time. Do you think you could help me move these boxes outside?
1229:At Éternité
1230:Huh? Move them out? Wait, what's going on, Reina?
1231:Hmm... Sad to say, but Éternité might be closed for the summer.
1232:Huh?! Why?!
1233:It's the heat and humidity. The coffee beans for our summer special were ruined during delivery.
1234:We had other food and drinks we could've served, but just our luck – the AC just gave up on us this morning.
1235:I'm not letting everyone work in such harsh conditions, and no one is going to sit down to eat in a sauna.
1236:Restocking and fixing the AC will take time. {var:player_nickname}, Hinata, I'll update you when we're back. My apologies...
1237:That look on Reina's face... I can't stop thinking about it.
1238:She's been working for the new blend since spring. Breaking a promise to her regulars is the last thing she wanted.
1239:Should we do something to help her out?
1240:Yeah... I just don't know how. If only I were as clever as you, {var:player_nickname}...
1241:Umm... {var:player_nickname}, could you help me out? Just like the way you handled things with Sprout Nursery!
1242:Hmm, let me see...
1243:What if we make a "summer special" that doesn't need any coffee beans at all?
1244:Oh! That would solve the whole restocking problem!
1245:But what should we make? Plain tea or juice might disappoint the regulars. It needs to be special.
1246:I know! {var:player_nickname}, you have so many friends in One Han City. Let's go ask them for ideas!
1247:Good plan. Let's see what we can find out!
1248:Saturne
1249:"The special flavor of summer," huh? Hahaha... You always come through with the most random questions, {var:player_nickname}.
1250:Summer's the only thing that can melt Northland's snow, but it's hard to describe the "flavor" of that.
1251:If I had to choose the most "honest" answer, though, I would have to say...
1252:...this "orange soda" right here.
1253:Wait, was that in your suit the whole time?!
1254:And it's just the basic kind from any old vending machine...
1255:A great businessman knows the best investments are often the most cost-effective ones.
1256:Real treasure is found in the simple things that trigger precious memories. When you've lived through the snow, you appreciate the sweetness.
1257:And who knows? An orange soda mixed by {var:player_nickname} might be something truly special.
1258:Haruna Igarashi
1259:The flavor of summer? Popsicles, obviously! Especially when you split one with a friend!
1260:And what's the flavor?
1261:Peach is sweet, Chocolate is so rich... My tummy loves them all! Don't make me pick!
1262:But I know this: if it's a good drink, it'll be an even better popsicle!
1263:I'm gotta go find the kitties! {var:player_nickname}, don't forget, you're coming with me next time!
1264:Yui Yagi
