1310:H-hey! No peeking!
1311:At least... not now. Maybe another time!
1312:Phew... Okay, tour's over. We have a drink to make! To the kitchen, {var:player_nickname}!
1313:Right, let's get to work.
1314:I'd love to see more...
1315:Ugh...
1316:I tried making it more bubbly, which completely washed out the flavor...
1317:Then I added orange zest and an orange popsicle as a garnish. It looks nice, but now it has this bitter taste I can't fix...
1318:I feel like I've tried everything I can think of, but it's just not working...
1319:It's okay... at least you did your best...
1320:I just... I really wanted this to work.
1321:But no matter what I do, I just can't find that "flavor of summer" we're looking for...
1322:Yeah, it feels like something is missing...
1323:Is there really nothing we can do until the next coffee beans arrive...?
1324:Maybe... we're trying too hard to find other people's "flavor of summer" instead of ours?
1325:What's your idea of summer?
1326:What's your favorite summer drink?
1327:Oh, me? Hmm...
1328:Besides the drinks on family trips... my grandma used to make me this cold drink when I was little.
1329:On those hot summer evenings with the cicadas buzzing... I'd sit on my little chair and watch her work in the garden.
1330:She'd hum these old songs I didn't know while rinsing the fresh-picked mint and basil. The whole yard would smell like them.
1331:Just when I was about to nod off from the heat, she'd hand me that drink...
1332:One sip of it felt like finding a patch of cool moss on a burning road, and just lying there to cool off...
1333:That's a very "Hinata" way to describe it.
1334:I don't know why, but that's the image that stuck. It was herbal and refreshingly cool just like the moss...
1335:But... don't all grandmas make drinks like that? It's probably nothing special...
1336:No, not all of them.
1337:Wait, really?!
1338:There's the clueless Hinata we know...
1339:Haha... Good thing you're here... otherwise I'd be making a fool of myself again.
1340:Still, that drink sounds unique, delicious, and simple... That's it! The perfect "summer special" Éternité needs!! Let's try to recreate it!
1341:Really? But... I don't have a recipe. I have no idea how she actually made it...
1342:We don't need a recipe if we have your memories. Let's work through it one step at a time!
1343:You said she washed the fresh mint and basil... What was her secret for getting that aroma out?
1344:Now that you mention it, I do remember a bit of what she did to them.
1345:She didn't chop them. She'd put the basil and mint in her palm and give them a light "clap"... That's how she woke up the aroma!
1346:There's the first step!
1347:The glass was always icy and full of bubbles... so we need chilled soda water!
1348:And the sweetness... she told me once it wasn't sugar, but I've totally forgotten what she used...
1349:...
1350:Hinata?
1351:Actually... Grandma left me a wooden box. She said her most precious things were inside.
1352:Sounds like a treasure box... Maybe the secret to the drink is in there!
1353:Hehe, I think so too. I was a bit scared to go through her things before... I didn't want to get sad again.
1354:But now, I've realized that remembering her doesn't have to be sad... What she left behind for me wasn't meant to be sorrow, but the joy within those memories.
1355:{var:player_nickname}, let's open it together.
1356:It's... dried mint, basil, and... stevia leaves? That must be the source of the sweetness! And there's a note underneath...
1357:{var:player_nickname}, I...
1358:It's okay.
1359:I'm right here with you.
1360:Okay...
1361:Note
1362:"To my dearest Hinata, who always gets woozy in the summer heat – "
1363:"If you ever miss my special drink, try this: 5 spearmint leaves, 3 sweet basil leaves, 2 stevia leaves. Clap them 'awake,' then add chilled soda and lemon."
1364:"I want you to learn this drink. That way, I'll always be by your side, and we'll share another joyful, unforgettable summer."
1365:She knew that eventually, some summer afternoon would lead me right back to this drink.
1366:I think... she wanted you to move forward. She left you a map to find her and recall the beautiful memories again.
1367:Alright, {var:player_nickname}. Let's make it!
1368:This time, I'm going to make "our" summer special using Grandma's recipe, so everyone can feel the same joy!
1369:Basil, stevia, lemon, mint... add the soda, a quick stir...
1370:All done! {var:player_nickname}, can you... do the honors?
